dx lint - run lint analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)

run lint analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)

Usage: dx lint|typecheck|format|generate [--apply] [--check] [--here] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

      --dry-run[=<DRY_RUN>]
          Show the plan without running it. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --quiet[=<QUIET>]
          Hide summaries. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -v, --verbose[=<VERBOSE>]
          Show more logs. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Set log level

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format

      --check
          Check without changing files

      --apply
          Consent to the writes or effects this command performs

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Fail on this severity

      --report <REPORT>
          Write a report file

      --here
          Use the current dir tree
          
          [alias: --cwd]

  -h, --help
          Print help

Per-command flags: --check/--apply/--fail-on/--report (quality only; --here for cwd scope; --output text|diff|json; unsupported uses fail with `option "--flag" is not supported by dx <command>`).

Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target, @repo//...), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Graph-scope commands select //... when no scope is supplied. Pass --here (--cwd alias) for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes and never changes the no-flag default.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|diff|json; --report sarif=<destination> (repeatable).
Rejected: --min-coverage, --debug, --release, --bazel, --prune-unobserved, --pin, --rollback, --configured, --from, --to, --serve, --port, --host, --open, --offline.
Environment: RUST_LOG=<filter> overrides --verbose and --log-level; NO_COLOR=<any> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

